The nettle backend of util/random.c seeds yarrow from getentropy(3), which is
not usable on Apple platforms or on Android:

    util/random.c: error: call to undeclared function 'getentropy'
    util/random.c: fatal error: 'sys/random.h' file not found

Darwin declares getentropy in <sys/random.h> rather than <unistd.h>, and
unbound declares it itself only where it also supplies an implementation --
which excludes both of these, because both have arc4random.  <sys/random.h>
in turn ships only in the macOS SDK: it is in neither the iPhoneOS nor the
iPhoneSimulator SDK, and Apple treats getentropy as private API outside
macOS, so using it gets an app rejected from the App Store however the
declaration is obtained.  Android's bionic declares it only from API level
28, so anything targeting older devices cannot see it either.

arc4random_buf(3) is public API on both, present far below any API level
worth targeting (21 on Android), drawn from the same system entropy, and
cannot fail -- so the error branch goes with it.  unbound already seeds
itself this way in its non-nettle configurations, and its own compat
arc4random is built where the platform lacks one.

The combination is untested upstream: an openssl or libbsd build takes the
arc4random branch of this file and never reaches the nettle one.

--- a/util/random.c
+++ b/util/random.c
@@ -189,6 +189,15 @@
 	/* Setup Yarrow context */
 	yarrow256_init(&s->ctx, 0, NULL);
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
+	/* getentropy(3) is not usable on either: Darwin declares it in <sys/random.h>, which ships
+	 * only in the macOS SDK, and treats the call as private API elsewhere; bionic declares it
+	 * only from API level 28.  arc4random_buf(3) is public on both, available for every API
+	 * level we build against, drawn from the same entropy, and cannot fail. */
+	arc4random_buf(buf, sizeof(buf));
+	yarrow256_seed(&s->ctx, YARROW256_SEED_FILE_SIZE, buf);
+	s->seeded = yarrow256_is_seeded(&s->ctx);
+#else
 	if(getentropy(buf, sizeof(buf)) != -1) {
 		/* got entropy */
 		yarrow256_seed(&s->ctx, YARROW256_SEED_FILE_SIZE, buf);
@@ -199,6 +208,7 @@
 		free(s);
 		return NULL;
 	}
+#endif
 
 	return s;
 }
